# 3 — MODIFICATION / AUTHORSHIP ATTENTION REGISTER

**Project attention:** Max Rupplin — MEARVK LLC — 2026

## Purpose

Record how project changes should be attributed when modifying existing kernel or driver code.

## Modification classes

### A. No project modification

Original source is retained. Existing attribution and license notices remain authoritative.

### B. Project modification

MEARVK changes source, configuration, build integration, interfaces, tests, or documentation. The original notices remain, and the project modification should be recorded clearly.

### C. Substantial project implementation

New functionality designed and implemented for Ubuntu Determinant may receive an explicit MEARVK authorship notice, while still declaring any incorporated third-party material.

## Required attention

Do not replace upstream author names with project names merely because the files now live in this repository.

For modified files, the preferred conceptual record is:

```text
Original authorship/licensing
        +
MEARVK modification, 2026
        +
current project maintenance attention
```

## Security-specific requirement

Security-sensitive modifications require additional review, testing, provenance, and concord verification before being represented as production-ready.